stateDiagram-v2
  state "Legend" as legend {
    direction LR
    lg0: Not installed, not built, or not started
    lg1: A step, a build or a tree as it should be
    lg2: Between: a check, a download, an install running
    lg3: A tree that differs from the release it names: a local build, fast-installed commits, a rollback
    lg4: Suspected open bug: the state that breaks the rule
    lg5: W1 open, CurrentIsLive and PatchLands: only install-release.sh moves releases/current, after install.sh (pack/install-release.sh 222-224). Going back by running the older release's install.sh, as pack/README.md 202 and install-release.sh 18-19 say, moves the units and leaves current on the newer one. fast-install then patches current's tree (scripts/fast-install 135-142), finds no unit in it (unit_dirs 355) or restarts units that run the other one, and says "fast-installed X onto VERSION". The next install keeps the wrong release as the one before (224-236), and get.sh reads the channel from it (get.sh 169-172) (red W1.1-3, TLC Rollback breaks in 12 steps, Fixed holds)
    lg6: W2 open, UnitsHaveFolder: a part a later install skips keeps its units in the old release's folder and container. Voice unticked or --no-voice, hands unticked, --no-hands, or --yes with no quiet sudo, which is FrameDrop with no password (install.sh 153-154). The units point at @REPO@ (hands/frametop-hands.service 16-19, frametop-camd.service 19, voice/frametop-voice.service 12, frametop-voice-whisper.service 14) and that tree's BOX (scripts/in-box). Two releases on, install-release.sh 225-236 removes the folder and the container, and those services fail. Only the recorders' menu entries are renewed (install.sh 174-176, 234-237) (red W2.1-3, TLC Skips breaks in 9 steps, Fixed holds)
    lg7: W3 open, ReleaseMatchesCommit, local builds only: ft dev build builds the image from the working tree (ft 188), uncommitted and untracked files in. .dockerignore leaves out a fixed list, not work/ or other untracked files. framedrop/build.sh 42 takes --commit from HEAD at pack time. fast-install diffs from that COMMIT (428-447) and trusts it for its rebuilds (490-491). A 0.3.0-local.SHA version is passed by hand, the repo doesn't make one. CI is clean: a fresh checkout and GITHUB_SHA (red W3.1-2, TLC Local breaks at once, CIOnly holds)
    lg8: W4 open, ReinstallGivesRelease: installing the same release again (the same IMAGE_ID) skips the copy when .frametop-release is there (install-release.sh 169-172, 193), so fast-installed files and .fast-install/ stay. The tree says COMMIT of the release and runs other commits. fast-install undo is the only way back (red W4.1-2, TLC Reinstall breaks in 8 steps, Fixed holds)
    lg9: W5 open, minor, NoMixedUnits and CurrentIsLive: install.sh runs 12 steps under set -e. A failing step or a power-off leaves the early steps' units in the new release and its container, the later ones in the old release, and current on the old one. fast-install then patches the old tree. The same command again finishes it: no copy, every step again (red W5.1-2, TLC Interrupt breaks in 3 to 7 steps, InstallSettles holds with the re-run, FixedInterrupt shows no other fix here helps)
    lg10: Holds at 78e93b1: TypeOK and InstallSettles in all 9 configs (116 to 155,405 states). Every rule in CIOnly (CI releases, full installs, no fast-install: 116) and Fixed (FixCurrent, FixSkip, FixReinstall, FixLocal, no interruption: 1844). The copy out of the image is atomic (VERSION.new, then mv), a damaged image file stops before anything is written (exit 3), another build under the same version is refused, and every model file is pinned to a commit and a sha256
    lg11: Escape hatches: W1, run the newest release's install-release.sh again. W2, install the skipped part again after each update (hands/run.sh install). W3, pack from a clean checkout, or use CI. W4, fast-install undo before installing again. W5, the same command again
    lg12: Another group: arrows into it are where a step reaches it, drawn there, not here
  }
