  state "The dev box and builds (setup/, scripts/, ft, pack/Containerfile)" as dv {
    b0: A source checkout: ~/frametop (get.sh clones it, ff-only updates), or a PC copy (scripts/sync.sh to ~/dev/frametop)
    [*] --> b0
    b1: Dev box "dev": a Fedora 44 toolbox through distrobox 1.8.2.5 (setup/dev-container.sh), started in a user scope by container-up.sh
    b2: Source install: install.sh builds each component in the dev box (its build.sh), the units point into the checkout
    b3: ft dev build: podman build -f pack/Containerfile from the working tree. Pinned: fedora-toolbox:44 by sha256, Python from uv.lock in /opt/frametop/venv, OpenVR v2.15.6 by sha256. .dockerignore leaves out .git, .worktrees, build/, captures, .env, testbench/, .claude/, fast-install, the tests, student and gaze models
    b4: ft dev test: the tests inside the image (justfile)
    b5: Image localhost/frametop:VERSION: the tree in /src/frametop, native binaries and the venv in /opt/frametop, the pinned hand student fetched in the build, no voice models
    b6: An image from a changed tree: uncommitted or untracked files in, under the commit HEAD names
  }
  state "CI (.github/workflows/release.yml)" as ci {
    c0: A v* tag or workflow_dispatch, on depot-ubuntu-24.04-arm-4
    [*] --> c0
    c1: Version: the tag minus v, else 0.0.0-ci.SHA7, FT_IMAGE=localhost/frametop:VERSION
    c2: ft dev build, ft dev test, then the smoke test: the binaries, the driver .so, hands/models.sh check, the distrobox, the venvs, zstd
    c3: framedrop/build.sh --image --version V --commit GITHUB_SHA
    c4: A draft release, a prerelease when the version has a -, notes with --release --experimental. Assets Frametop.zip, frametop.framedrop.json, frametop-release.json, SHA256SUMS. A manual run keeps them 7 days as an artifact
    c5: Published by hand: stable is Latest, experimental a prerelease
  }
  state "Pack (framedrop/build.sh, pack/release-info.py)" as pk {
    k0: podman save: frametop-image.tar, an OCI archive
    [*] --> k0
    k1: frametop-release.json (frametop.release/v1): version, commit, channel (experimental when the version has a -), the image file's sha256 and the image ID, the SteamOS table from pack/steamos.json
    k2: Frametop.zip, about 1.1 GB, fixed dates so it rebuilds byte for byte: the image, the release JSON, install-release.sh, the FrameDrop installer, get.sh, with a framedrop.install/v1 manifest and SHA256SUMS
    k3: A local pack: the version picked by hand, such as 0.3.0-local.SHA, installed with get.sh --zip
    k4: A test zip without --image: get.sh inside, it installs from source
  }
  state "The ways in (get.sh, framedrop/installer)" as wi {
    i0: get.sh: a menu (stable, experimental, a version, from source), Frametop/frametop. Stable from releases/latest, experimental the newest non-draft release with a Frametop.zip, --version V the tag vV. A resumable download to ~/.cache/frametop/release
    [*] --> i0
    i1: FrameDrop: Steam runs frametop-install.sh, which leaves pressure-vessel through flatpak-spawn. progress.py runs install-release.sh --yes, and --no-voice, --no-hands, --no-hand-recorder, --no-eye-tracker from its boxes, in the user service frametop-framedrop-install. The password goes over an askpass socket (peer and cgroup checked), none and the sudo parts are skipped
    i2: The zip unpacked: frametop-install.sh, or install-release.sh by hand
    i3: get.sh from source: clone or ff-only update ~/frametop, then ./install.sh
  }
  state "install-release.sh (pack/)" as ir {
    r0: check_release: tested, untested (asks unless --yes), broken (stops unless --any-steamos). The newest table from GitHub main, offline the zip's own
    [*] --> r0
    r1: Load: 5 GB free, sha256sum -c (damaged: exit 3, get.sh drops the zip), podman load, tag. The same image ID loaded already: skipped
    r2: Copy: /src/frametop out of the image into VERSION.new, write .frametop-release (VERSION, COMMIT, CHANNEL, IMAGE, IMAGE_ID, BOX=frametop-ID12), mv. Another IMAGE_ID in VERSION is refused
    r3: Run VERSION/install.sh
    r4: Done: current -> VERSION. Every release but this one and the one current named before goes, with its container and image
    r5: The folder was there (the same IMAGE_ID): nothing copied, fast-installed files kept
  }
  state "install.sh (12 steps, set -e)" as is {
    s0: Steps 1-2: the distrobox the image brings, release-box.sh makes frametop-ID12 from the image and checks the ID again. A clone: the dev box
    [*] --> s0
    s1: Steps 3-7, always: relay, pointer driver, helper and dashpatch, power, screens and the desktop session, Full Keyboard, the settings apps, the tour, Remote Displays, conf-migrate.sh. Units at @REPO@ (this tree), programs through scripts/in-box and BOX
    s2: Steps 8-12, optional: voice, hands (sudo: ft-camd's capabilities), gaze, our eye tracker (sudo: /etc/frametop/ft-eyegrab), Bluetooth (sudo, the /etc keep list). The recorders' menu entries renewed
    s3: Every unit runs this tree, SteamVR restart offered
    s4: Stopped mid-way: the early units in the new release, the later ones in the old, current on the old
    s5: A part skipped this time: its units still in an older release's folder and container
    s6: That folder and container removed two releases on: the services fail
    s7: Rolled back: the units run the older tree, current still names the newer one
  }
  state "fast-install (scripts/fast-install, left out of the image)" as fi {
    f0: A commit on experimental
    [*] --> f0
    f1: Diff from the COMMIT of current's tree, in a --shared clone in ~/.cache/frametop-fast/src. Rebuilds changed components in the release's box (frame-job --local, taskset). Image changes refused unless --partial. A flock
    f2: In place: originals to .fast-install/orig, state.json (commit, at). Restarts the units using the tree, the desktop not while worn (--worn-ok). An installer's changes and a held ft-camd listed as steps left (exit 3)
    f3: status, undo (the release as it was), done PATH
    f4: Patched a tree nothing runs: "fast-installed X onto VERSION", the running units unchanged
  }
  state "The models (models/, hands/models.sh, voice/models.sh)" as md {
    m0: Hands student pinned in hands/models.pin (format 1, rev 03d7695, v20a), fetched by hands/build.sh into hands/models/student. The stock MediaPipe ncnn models are in the tree
    [*] --> m0
    m1: hands/models.json: HANDS_MODEL latest, stock or a version, from Hugging Face DeeJanuz/frametop-hands-models into the tree's hands/models/versions
    m2: gaze/tracker/models.json: EYES_MODEL classic, latest or a version, from DeeJanuz/frametop-eyes-models into gaze/tracker/models
    m3: ft-models auto at service start: the catalog from GitHub raw, the branch by channel (.frametop-release CHANNEL, a clone's own branch), at most every 15 min. Each file pinned to a Hugging Face commit and a sha256, format gated
    m4: voice/models.sh: about 340 MB into ~/.local/share/frametop/voice/models, shared by every release: whisper small.en q5_1, Moonshine base, kws zipformer, silero VAD, from fixed Hugging Face and sherpa-onnx URLs with sha256
  }
  state "Upkeep (scripts/, uninstall.sh)" as up {
    u0: update-check.py: SteamOS drift against what Frametop leans on, read-only, --mark-good
    [*] --> u0
    u1: uninstall.sh: two steps around a restart. The units, the driver, the /etc files, the capabilities, then every release with its container and image, and the dev box
    u2: conf-migrate.sh: frametop.conf lines that still read as an older example wrote them, and rules-migrate.py's one-time key bindings
  }
